    "introductoryText": "For each input record, takes a screenshot of the Report tab (or other web page) at the record's URL and posts it to one Slack channel, with the record's message and a link to the page (added unless the message already holds it). Optionally the screenshots are also combined into one PDF, posted after them.\n\n**How to set it up**: choose the URL field and the message field, the screenshot size and orientation. Create a Slack app at [api.slack.com/apps](https://api.slack.com/apps), give its bot the `files:write` scope, install it in your workspace and add it to the channel (`/invite @your-app`). Paste the **Bot User OAuth token** (`xoxb-...`) and the **channel ID** (in the channel's details, such as `C0123ABCD`).\n\nThe first output has one record per input record: posted, skipped (no URL) or error, with Slack's file ID; the second lists the errors. A record that fails doesn't stop the others; if nothing at all is posted, the block stops with the first error.\n\n**What it needs.** Chrome, driven by the `visokio-omniprint` Python package (installed on first run). On a server that runs custom blocks in Docker, the block uses its own image with Chrome included ([Docker setup](https://help.visokio.com/support/solutions/articles/42000071133-setting-up-the-custom-block)); otherwise Chrome must be installed on the machine running Omniscope. Each page must be reachable from that machine.\n\n**Authentication.** For pages behind Basic Authentication (for example a Report with Local Desktop Experience turned off), enter a username and password. They are used only to open the page; they are not written to the output.",
